row=("| 2026-11-11 | UNIQUE MOVES batch 4 (branch g-moves4, on ii-dlc 2e7190ca; not pushed; no relay) | The owner: every fighter's moves should be their own. Batch 4 covers the up specials, smashes, neutral specials AND down specials for the ten main-cast fighters the new similarity audit (scripts/_m4/an4.py: for up and smash the shape or pattern plus the share of numbers within 15%; for neutral and down special the token skeleton of the code, 60%, and the share of numbers within 15%, 40%) ranked most alike to another fighter's, excluding the 30 already done in batches 1-3: Ruby (3.01 total of four slots: down and neutral shared with Gelatin-style floor traps and Fanny's line), Firey Jr., Bell and TV (identical down-special code: armour plus a stun ring), Ruler and Coiny (counter stances, Coiny's identical to Firey's), Gelatin, Loser, Fern, Fanny. NEW MOVES (16; reports/moves-batch4.csv has the old and new of each): Ruby down Shard Spray (three bouncing gem shards), smash Facet Fall (two crystals drop on the nearest foe); Firey Jr. down Flare Up (flame ring, burns), up Fire Whirl (spin, burns); Bell down Toll (armour then a slowing toll, no damage); TV down Pause (after a wind-up roots the nearest foe 34 frames), neutral Scan Lines (two bars of static); Ruler down Straight Edge (reflects shots 22 frames); Gelatin down Jelly Bounce (hop over a foe, untouchable 12, a rooting blob left); Loser down Shrug It Off (clears every status, 6 healing, armour 30), smash Cold Snap (ring of chill, ices); Fern smash Root Down (plant, roots foes); Coiny down Spare Change (three coins); Fanny neutral Gust (also shoves foes ahead) and smash Cyclone (a whirlwind through everyone). Locks stay under the cap (TV 34, Fern 40), no root outlasts a stun, up specials take no tell, the new smashes keep their smash charge, Bell's and TV's rings keep the 8-frame wind-up. CANON: all design bases, NONE checked against an episode (the csv says so per row); Fern's pole jump (kept) is the one canon line. MEASURED SIMILARITY, before to after (total of the four best matches): Ruby 3.01 to 2.27, Firey Jr. 2.98 to 2.47, Bell 2.97 to 2.22, TV 2.97 to 2.03, Ruler 2.75 to 2.57, Gelatin 2.75 to 2.33, Loser 2.75 to 2.30, Fern 2.74 to 2.78 (WORSE: Root Down is a plant like Sidewalky's, smash 0.64 to 0.67; not fixed), Coiny 2.74 to 2.46, Fanny 2.72 to 2.01. Two new look-alikes of my own: Ruby's and Coiny's down specials are both a three-projectile fan (0.73); Gelatin's and Firey Jr.'s neutral lobs stay 0.85 (left alone). Ruler only got one slot (his others are canon-shaped or core), Bell one (her smash and up were only 0.60 alike). CHECKS: every changed move fired at 60, 140 and 230 px on a still foe (scripts/_m4/fire.mjs): 15 moves, 0 errors, each hit at its natural range; Straight Edge turned a shot back (Pen took the 6; without it Ruler took it); other 101 roster rows (up, smash, names, texts, brain, down code, end lag) identical, and a seeded 1500-frame match of four unchanged fighters is identical before and after WITH A FAKE CLOCK (scripts/_m4/noop4.mjs; without it the match differs run to run even on one build, so the batch-3 check was clock-blind); syntax: the two script blocks pass node --check (there is no 'syncheck' script in the repo; this was my substitute); boot check clean (ffa and teams bad positions 0, errors none, control bytes 0, bare LF 0, hidden names none, kit guard ok). BRAIN_SPEC re-measured for the kits whose near/far/damage/carry changed (beam, emberjr, ring, static, freeze, cool, slap; scripts/_m4/brain.mjs, the method reproduces the old table to within the first row's 10-px start). Fighter pages for the ten regenerated (gen-seo-pages, date left 2026-11-09, CRLF; the other 119 rewritten files restored). BALANCE PANEL (mid-top: each against Fries, Lollipop, Match, Naily, Toothpaste, Rocky, Firey, Pen in turn, both Expert, 1v1, 3 stocks, 1800-frame cap, 32 matches per version, before and after in ONE process per fighter, BelowNormal, same seeds, scripts/_m4/panel.mjs): wins before to after: Ruby 18 to 19, Firey Jr. 19 to 16, Bell 4 to 4, TV 6 to 8, Ruler 31 to 28, Gelatin 11 to 18, Loser 6 to 2, Fern 4 to 5, Coiny 8 to 7, Fanny 23 to 21 (of 32). NOISE: one fighter's 32 is about plus or minus 5.5 wins at the 95% level in the middle, so a before/after gap of under 8 wins is noise; only Gelatin (+7) and Loser (-4 from a low base) are near it, and neither is reliable. No result was used to tune a move. Loser is the weakest of the ten and got slightly weaker on paper (2/32), Bell 4/32 and Fern 5/32 stay near the bottom; the owner may want a buff pass. KNOWN GAPS: nothing was seen in a browser (new shapes use the old poses); the panel's process ran out of memory once (a jsdom leak) and was rerun one fighter per process; a late jsdom error after window close prints at the end of each process (3 lines, not from a match); one run was interrupted by an app restart and resumed at TV with Ruby, Firey Jr. and Bell kept. |\n")
